  "answers": {
    "vision": {
      "answer": "Non-A-rated articles consistently outnumber A-rated articles and generally rise over time, from about 8,000 in 2000 to roughly 10,000 by 2010–2011. A-rated articles remain comparatively stable at around 5,000–6,000 per year, so the gap between the two groups widens.",
